Ezekiel: Pits are too close together. They're stealing from each other.
Ezekiel: Fill every second one. You'll get more from half of them than all of them, and I know how that sounds.
Ezekiel: This ground's different from mine. Sand — water goes straight through it.
Ezekiel: Mulch matters more here than pits do. Heavy mulch, and manure deeper than I'd normally say.
Ezekiel: ...You've been doing three-quarters of this already. Your mother's way?
Ezekiel: Then the only thing I've got for you is the pits, and you'll tell me in a season whether they're worth the digging.
